Spec: Android owner-side native verification fixture

Purpose:
  Exercise real Keystore, descriptors and owner state without exposing test administration in the production APK.

Owns:
  ./NativeOwnerTest.java

Must:
  Keep fixture commands inside instrumentation and target-private files; production components gain no test API.
  Export only a CSR and public evidence, prove the Keystore key cannot be encoded and validate descriptor half-close and blocked-read disposal.
  Bound the owner host to five minutes and stop its foreground runtime on fixture exit.

  Permit explicit fixture server configuration while stopped and export only the current public APK signing fingerprint for independent SDK pinning.

  Verify corrupted saved server configuration cannot publish a preview runtime and that owner stop prevents a late startup from becoming active.

  Report only aggregate owned runtime counts for scope-sharing acceptance; no production Binder management is added.
  Report aggregate selected LAN and XTCP counts so the coordinator does not infer the direct candidate from the emulator topology.

  Repeat immediate start/stop/start requests and observe beyond the foreground timeout window; a framework crash fails acceptance rather than being hidden by a successful earlier RPC.

  Preserve the exact optional STUN destination snapshot across private server configuration persistence.
  Permit an instrumentation-only generation invalidation command and aggregate formal XTCP count without adding production management transactions or changing device networking.
  Permit an explicit owner fixture peer-route revision to a held silent loopback listener so cold XTCP is tested without accidental LAN success or external negative targets.
  Verify reliable descriptor abort is distinguishable from clean EOF using an original descriptor after duplicated read handles.
